change:
  id: CHG-019
  title: Put the accepted contract on the wired promotion path
  status: delivered
  intent: Let an operator declare a mutation contract for a run, validate it, and carry it through the loop to the contract-aware scorer, so declared required_evidence gates a live promotion and RISK-002 can close.
  audience_level: developer
  relates_to:
    - RISK-002
    - ARCH-001
    - CON-002
    - SYS-001

deltas:
  - op: MODIFIED
    capability: mutation-fitness-loop
    requirement: A run may carry an operator-declared contract, and when it does the declared required_evidence ids gate promotion on the wired path.
    scenarios:
      - id: S1
        when: an operator declares a required_evidence id and the run produces a passing check of that name
        then: the declared gate contributes no discard and scoring proceeds
      - id: S2
        when: an operator declares a required_evidence id and no check of that name is produced
        then: the candidate is discarded on a gate naming that id, because absent evidence is not passing evidence
      - id: S3
        when: an operator declares a required_evidence id and a check of that name fails
        then: the candidate is discarded on a gate naming that id
      - id: S4
        when: a run declares no contract
        then: it behaves exactly as before, reaching the contractless scorer entry point with the existing structural gates
      - id: S5
        when: an operator declares a contract the validator rejects, such as an unsupported operator or an unsafe locus
        then: the run stops before any candidate is created and reports why
      - id: S6
        when: a declared contract is carried through the loop
        then: the same contract instance reaches the scorer, so what gated the candidate is what the operator declared
        and:
          - a check the contract did not declare cannot satisfy a declared id

acceptance:
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: cli/EvolveContractAcceptanceTest.promotesWhenEveryDeclaredEvidenceCheckPasses
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: cli/EvolveContractAcceptanceTest.discardsWhenADeclaredEvidenceCheckIsAbsent
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: cli/EvolveContractAcceptanceTest.discardsWhenADeclaredEvidenceCheckFails
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S4
    test_id: cli/EvolveContractAcceptanceTest.aRunWithoutAContractIsUnchanged
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S5
    test_id: cli/EvolveContractAcceptanceTest.refusesAContractTheValidatorRejects
    layer: acceptance
  - scenario: S6
    test_id: deterministic/MutationEvaluationLoopContractTest.carriesTheDeclaredContractToTheScorer
    layer: unit

tasks:
  - id: T1
    slice: map declared required_evidence ids onto named check outcomes, producing RequiredEvidenceResult values from EvaluationEvidence
    status: completed
  - id: T2
    slice: add the failing acceptance and unit coverage for S1 through S6
    status: completed
  - id: T3
    slice: carry an optional contract through MutationEvaluationLoop and widen the FitnessScorer port to accept it
    status: completed
  - id: T4
    slice: expose operator, required evidence and bounds as saaa-evolve options, validated by MutationContractValidator before any candidate is created
    status: completed
  - id: T5
    slice: keep the everyOperatorSharesTheObjectiveSetTheScorerAssumes tripwire and correct the retirement condition CHG-014 recorded, which was too loose
    status: completed
    note: CHG-014 said to retire it once the wired path was contract-aware. The wired path is contract-aware only when a contract is declared; a run without --operator still reaches the contractless entry point, which still weights against DEFAULT_OBJECTIVES. Retiring the tripwire would therefore remove the only guard against a per-operator objective set silently producing a wrong weighted score on every contractless run. The correct condition is that the contractless entry point no longer exists
  - id: T6
    slice: narrow RISK-002 to the contractless path, update CHG-002 T4b and T4c, README, wiki and the CHG-014 records that describe the gap as open
    status: completed

non_goals:
  - the TOON envelope parser or any model-emitted contract; CHG-002 T3d is unaffected
  - making behavioral_safety vary or adding further evidence sources
  - ranking, population, or any change to objective weights or the promotion threshold
  - removing the contractless entry point, which stays for callers that supply no contract

risks:
  - a declared evidence id must be lower snake_case because it becomes a subject.invariant audit key, while check names in this repository are hyphenated by convention. An operator declaring required evidence must therefore name that check to match the id exactly. Translating hyphens to underscores silently was rejected: an unwritten naming convention between two modules already caused one silent failure in CHG-016
  - declaring an operator commits the run to that operator's own required evidence, so `--operator repair` demands failing_case_reproduced, unit_tests_pass and regression_case_added. That is the intent rather than a side effect, but it means adopting a contract on an existing target usually means renaming or adding checks
  - hill-climb and exploratory-leap need a search posture, which has no options yet, so declaring them is rejected with that reason rather than producing a contract the validator would refuse later with a worse message
  - widening the FitnessScorer port touches every implementor, and the port is the seam CHG-014's S9 asserts cannot carry a contract. That test must be replaced rather than deleted, or the gap it guards stops being visible while it is still partly open
  - mapping declared evidence onto check names couples a contract's vocabulary to whatever the operator named their scripts. A typo in either place produces a discard rather than a silent pass, which is the safe direction, but the diagnostic must name the id so the cause is obvious
  - an operator can declare a contract that is trivially satisfiable, for example requiring only a check that always passes. The contract bounds the model, not the operator, and nothing here changes that
